# TTP-2026-0099 — Sign-In Behavioral Anomaly on a Learned Identity Baseline — Cortex Analytics Behavioral IOC (ABIOC) (T1078.004 / T1110.004)
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## ABIOC — ITDR-009 Sign-In Auth-Velocity and New-ASN Deviation from Learned Identity Baseline (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Learned per-identity sign-in baseline (stable ASN set, human auth cadence) -> valid-account authentication from a new autonomous system at an anomalous velocity that diverges from the baseline, anchored to the originating auth event.
# A user whose learned Cortex sign-in profile is a narrow, stable set of source ASNs at a human auth cadence suddenly authenticates successfully from an autonomous system absent from the baseline, at a velocity the account never exhibits. Every credential is valid and no single IP is a known-bad IOC; the ABIOC fires on the ASN-and-velocity deviation from the account's learned behavior, anchored to the valid-account causality chain rather than to any static indicator.

dataset = okta_sso
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 1800)
| filter eventType = "user.session.start" and auth_outcome = "SUCCESS"
| comp count() as success_count, count_distinct(src_asn) as distinct_asns, values(src_asn) as asns, earliest(_time) as first_seen, latest(_time) as last_seen by actor_effective_username
| alter window_minutes = divide(subtract(last_seen, first_seen), 60000000)
| filter distinct_asns >= 2 and success_count >= 5 and window_minutes <= 60
| fields actor_effective_username, success_count, distinct_asns, asns, window_minutes, first_seen, last_seen

## ABIOC — ITDR-009 Impossible-Travel Geo-Velocity Deviation from Learned Sign-In Baseline (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: New-ASN valid-account auth -> a second successful session from a geographically distant location inside a travel-impossibility window that exceeds the account's learned single-region geography, anchored to the session pair from one intrusion.
# The same user succeeds at two sign-ins from geographically distant locations inside a travel-impossibility window, deviating from the single-region geography Cortex learned for the account. The credentials are valid and each session in isolation is benign; the ABIOC fires on the geo-velocity deviation from the learned sign-in profile, anchored to the session pair spawned by the same stolen-credential intrusion.

dataset = msft_azure_ad_signin
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 1800)
| filter auth_outcome = "SUCCESS"
| comp count_distinct(src_geo_country) as geo_count, count_distinct(src_asn) as asn_count, values(src_geo_city) as cities, earliest(_time) as first_seen, latest(_time) as last_seen by user_name
| alter window_minutes = divide(subtract(last_seen, first_seen), 60000000)
| filter geo_count >= 2 and window_minutes <= 300
| sort desc geo_count
| fields user_name, geo_count, asn_count, cities, window_minutes, first_seen, last_seen

## VALIDATION — ITDR-009 Learned Sign-In Baseline Present
# purpose: validation
# dataset: okta_sso

dataset = okta_sso
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 604800)
| filter eventType = "user.session.start" and auth_outcome = "SUCCESS"
| comp count_distinct(src_asn) as baseline_asns, count_distinct(src_geo_country) as baseline_countries by actor_effective_username
| filter baseline_asns >= 1
| fields actor_effective_username, baseline_asns, baseline_countries

## VALIDATION — ITDR-009 Anomalous Session Pair Surfaced
# purpose: validation
# dataset: okta_sso

dataset = okta_sso
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 1800)
| filter eventType = "user.session.start" and auth_outcome = "SUCCESS"
| comp count() as success_count, count_distinct(src_asn) as distinct_asns by actor_effective_username
| filter distinct_asns >= 2 and success_count >= 2
| fields actor_effective_username, success_count, distinct_asns

